# heimdall runtime state — per-checkout local state, never commit.
# Holds user data (agent_history, token budget, conflict_log) and is the store
# the pre-push quality gate reads. It is created by `heimdall-state init`, so it
# is absent in a fresh clone and in every agent worktree — that absence is normal,
# not a setup failure. Ignored under both the current and legacy (superx) names;
# the rename left the heimdall name untracked-but-unignored, which showed up as
# permanent `git status` noise for every user.
heimdall-state.json
heimdall-state.json.lock
# superx runtime state — never commit, contains user data
superx-state.json
superx-state.json.lock
superx-session.json
superx-history.json
superx-checkpoint.json
superx-github.json
superx-workspace/
# claude-code internals
.claude/agent-memory/
# user-generated docs (research/plans/specs from real tasks)
docs/analysis/
docs/superpowers/plans/
# guard install output — per-clone local git-hooks dir wired via core.hooksPath
# (`hmd guard install`). Install output, not source. Lives in the working tree
# (not .git/) on purpose so a relative core.hooksPath survives a repo move.
# Also holds the SI-2 attestation runtime store (.heimdall/attestations/<id>.json):
# one record per commit/task, emitted by `heimdall-attest` and read by F2–F6 —
# per-checkout runtime state, never committed.
# Ignore the runtime home's CONTENTS (so the real config + secrets + the
# attestation store never commit) — but as `.heimdall/*` (not `.heimdall/`) so
# git still DESCENDS into the dir and the single un-ignore below can take effect.
.heimdall/*
.heimdall/attestations/
# The telemetry NDJSON event store (.heimdall/telemetry/events*.ndjson): per-
# checkout runtime metrics, local-first, NEVER committed. Already covered by
# `.heimdall/*` above; named explicitly so a future un-ignore exception can never
# accidentally leak it. The store stays gitleaks-CLEAN-by-construction (the scrubber
# keeps secrets out) — it is NEVER added to .gitleaks.toml's allowlist.
.heimdall/telemetry/
# EXCEPTION: the issue-loop config EXAMPLE is committed source (structure +
# env-var NAMES only, never secrets). The REAL config (.heimdall/issue-loop.config.json)
# and secrets file stay ignored by `.heimdall/*`; only this single .example is
# un-ignored so it can be committed.
!.heimdall/issue-loop.config.json.example
# EXCEPTION: the control-plane endpoint EXAMPLE is committed source (shape + env-var
# NAMES only, never a real url/token). The REAL config + the per-dev signing seeds
# stay ignored (below); only this single .example is un-ignored so it can be committed.
!.heimdall/cp-endpoint.json.example
# CONTROL-PLANE PRESENCE SECRETS — the per-dev CP endpoint config (url + enroll TOKEN)
# and the Ed25519 signing SEEDS. The canonical store is $HOME/.heimdall — OUT of any
# dev repo — but $HOME/.heimdall IS the installed plugin clone (a checkout of THIS
# repo), so these land at the clone's repo ROOT, which `.heimdall/*` above does NOT
# cover. Ignore them at the root so a stray `git add .` in the install clone can NEVER
# stage a dev's enroll token or seed. (The .example template above is the only
# committed form; the real token lives 0600 in $HOME, never tracked.)
/cp-endpoint.json
/pki/
/identity.json
/team.json
/*.seed
# Belt-and-suspenders for a dev who creates them under an in-repo .heimdall/ (already
# covered by `.heimdall/*`, named here so an un-ignore exception can never leak them).
# team.json is the per-repo TEAM SECRET — a bearer capability. RECONCILIATION (settled
# model): it stays GITIGNORED by default (this line) so a stray `git add .` can NEVER
# stage the secret; the DELIBERATE private-repo path in bin/heimdall-team FORCE-ADDS it
# (`git add -f`, --no-verify) ONLY after PROVING the repo private (read access == the
# team boundary → clone == join). Once tracked, gitignore no longer applies to it. A
# PUBLIC / privacy-unverifiable repo keeps it ignored and grows the team via `hmd invite`.
.heimdall/cp-endpoint.json
.heimdall/pki/
.heimdall/identity.json
.heimdall/team.json
.heimdall/*.seed
# TEAM AUTO-JOIN — team.shared.json is the TRACKED, committed-in-a-PRIVATE-repo team
# secret that lets collaborators auto-join (unlike team.json, the personal/gitignored
# secret). It is committed ONLY in a verified-private repo — bin/heimdall-team refuses
# to write it for a public/unverifiable origin (the leak guard), so it never carries a
# secret into a repo whose own access control is not proven. Un-ignore it past
# `.heimdall/*` and the root-level `/team.json` so `git add -f` can track it.
!.heimdall/team.shared.json
!/team.shared.json
